HST Office: a picture saved as .rtf keeps its shown size (Word's whole-percent \picscalex).

The RTF export wrote a picture's size as its original size (\picwgoal / \pichgoal) times a scale (\picscalex /
\picscaley) that RTF keeps as a whole percent, so a picture shown at 65.9 % was written at 65 % and came back 1-2 %
smaller after every save (s037: 20 pictures, together with the next patch two pages short of Word). An uncropped
picture now gets its shown size as the goal, at 100 %; a cropped one keeps its original size as the goal, as before,
since its crops are in those units (sw/source/filter/ww8/hst/rtfpicturescale.cxx).

Test: CppunitTest_sw_rtfexport8 testHstPictureShownSizeKept (a picture at 65.9 % round-trips within 1 twip).

